{"id":"2ca7fe0e0761b8f4c09beddcf29bc0a4b071c842","axis":"silent","repo":"symfony/symfony","sha":"2ca7fe0e0761b8f4c09beddcf29bc0a4b071c842","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"UPGRADE-8.2.md","lines":["@@ -149,6 +149,7 @@ FrameworkBundle","  * Deprecate the `framework.ide` config option, use the `SYMFONY_IDE` env var instead","  * Deprecate passing the `$debug` argument to `DependencyInjection\\Configuration::__construct()`, the config tree no longer depends on `kernel.debug`","  * BrowserKit assertions are no longer verbose by default. Failed response assertions no longer include the response body unless `setBrowserKitAssertionsAsVerbose(true)` is called or `verbose: true` is passed to the assertion.","+ * `MailerAssertionsTrait` and `NotificationAssertionsTrait` now see the emails and notifications sent during the previous requests of the test client. They used to see only the ones sent during the last request. A test that expects no email after a second request must now account for the emails sent before it","  * Deprecate the `framework.fragments.hinclude_default_template` config option and the `fragment.renderer.hinclude.global_template` parameter; use the `esi` or `inline` fragment renderer, or [Symfony UX Turbo](https://ux.symfony.com/turbo), instead","  * Most of what this bundle configured now lives in a bundle shipped by the component itself: `asset`,","    `asset_mapper`, `cache`, `html_sanitizer`, `http_client`, `json_streamer`, `lock`, `mailer`, `messenger`,"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Symfony/Bundle/FrameworkBundle/CHANGELOG.md","lines":["@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@ CHANGELOG"," 8.2"," ---"," ","+ * Make `MailerAssertionsTrait` and `NotificationAssertionsTrait` see the emails and notifications sent during the previous requests of the test client","  * Add the `kernel.test_state` tag to call a method of a service when a test ends, or to keep a copy of the service before each reset until the test ends","  * Pass the token of `KernelBrowser::loginUser()` with each request, so that stateless firewalls can read it","  * Inject the `clock` service into the session `MetadataBag`"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Symfony/Bundle/FrameworkBundle/Test/MailerAssertionsTrait.php","lines":["@@ -135,7 +135,21 @@ private static function getMessageMailerEvents(): MessageEvents","     {","         $container = static::getContainer();","         if ($container->has('mailer.message_logger_listener')) {","-            return $container->get('mailer.message_logger_listener')->getEvents();","+            $listener = $container->get('mailer.message_logger_listener');","+","+            if (!$container instanceof TestContainer || !$keptListeners = $container->getKeptState('mailer.message_logger_listener')) {","+                return $listener->getEvents();","+            }","+","+            $events = new MessageEvents();","+","+            foreach ([...$keptListeners, $listener] as $someListener) {","+                foreach ($someListener->getEvents()->getEvents() as $event) {","+                    $events->add($event);","+                }","+            }","+","+            return $events;","         }"," ","         static::fail('A client must have Mailer enabled to make email assertions. Did you forget to require symfony/mailer?');"],"additions":15,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Symfony/Bundle/FrameworkBundle/Test/NotificationAssertionsTrait.php","lines":["@@ -92,7 +92,21 @@ public static function getNotificationEvents(): NotificationEvents","     {","         $container = static::getContainer();","         if ($container->has('notifier.notification_logger_listener')) {","-            return $container->get('notifier.notification_logger_listener')->getEvents();","+            $listener = $container->get('notifier.notification_logger_listener');","+","+            if (!$container instanceof TestContainer || !$keptListeners = $container->getKeptState('notifier.notification_log